# The checks of the team's own project (own_project in bin/lib/team.sh) that no merge waits on:
# their findings show on a PR and are fixed in a task of their own, and neither a red nor a pending
# one holds a PR, a merge or the merge queue. A committed constant, never a registry key, since
# the registry is a record any session can edit.
# One line each: the workflow's file name under .github/workflows/, one space, the check's name
# (its job's). On a PR's head or a trial commit, team-ci-wait neither waits on such a check or its
# workflow's run nor fails on it (with --run it passes over none), and pr_part (team-state,
# team-merge, team-catch-up) keeps it out of the passed, failing and pending checks. No other
# project's check of the same name is passed over, and neither is a name the project's
# required_checks require; pr_part holds one the PR's server-required checks or the base's rules
# require too, and team-ci-wait holds the rules' once it has read them, on a PR's head (but with
# --look) and with --merge-group, the modes that read them.
# Each workflow runs on pull requests and by hand, never on a merge queue's trial commit, and no
# job of it is a required check, which tests/repo.bats holds.
rust-macos.yml rust-macos
